  "name": "METHYLMALONIC ACID QUANTITATIVE SERUM",
  "code": "1778",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>1. Diet, nutritional status &amp; age should be considered in the evaluation of urine MMA levels.<br>2. Organic acid quantitation by Tandem Mass Spectrometry is recommended in children for all positive results<br>3. Results should be clinically correlated as individual / biological variations can affect the test results</p>\n<p><strong>Comments&nbsp;</strong>:<br>Vitamin B12 can be detected through estimation of Methylmalonic Acid (MMA) even when deficiency symptoms of Vitamin B12 are present in&nbsp;an individual but serum B12 levels are normal. MMA is a sensitive indicator which detects early Vitamin B12 deficiency. In pediatric patients,&nbsp;elevated MMA values indicate a probable Methylmalonic acidemia wheras in adults, it is indicative of cobalamin deficiency.</p>",
